      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "PART A: EARTHQUAKES"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Earthquakes originate at the Focus (Hypocentre) underground, while the point directly above it on the surface is called the Epicentre.",
        "Seismic waves are divided into Body Waves (P-waves and S-waves) which travel through the interior, and Surface Waves which move along the crust.",
        "Earthquake magnitude (energy released) is measured by the Richter scale, while intensity (damage caused) is measured by the Mercalli scale.",
        "Volcanoes are classified by activity status (Active, Dormant, Extinct) and by shape (Shield, Composite, Cinder Cone, Caldera).",
        "The Circum-Pacific Belt, known as the Ring of Fire, contains the highest concentration of global seismic and volcanic activity."
      ],
      "id": "ozdnxnb"
    },
