    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Primary (P) waves are longitudinal and travel through solids, liquids, and gases, whereas Secondary (S) waves are transverse and travel only through solids.",
        "The Richter Scale is logarithmic and measures energy magnitude, while the Mercalli Scale measures observable damage intensity from I to XII.",
        "Basaltic lava is fluid and forms low-sloped Shield Volcanoes, whereas Viscous/Andesitic lava causes explosive eruptions forming Composite Volcanoes."
